1
00:00:02,258 --> 00:00:04,427
KATARA: Water.

2
00:00:04,844 --> 00:00:06,304
Earth.

3
00:00:06,596 --> 00:00:08,598
Fire.

4
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:10,308
Air.

5
00:00:11,142 --> 00:00:15,104
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,438 --> 00:00:19,275
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,776 --> 00:00:22,403
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:22,529 --> 00:00:23,738
could stop them.

9
00:00:23,863 --> 00:00:26,699
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

10
00:00:27,367 --> 00:00:29,494
A hundred years passed,
and my brother and I discovered

11
00:00:29,577 --> 00:00:32,664
the new Avatar, an airbender named Aang.

12
00:00:32,956 --> 00:00:35,166
And although
his airbending skills are great,

13
00:00:35,291 --> 00:00:37,585
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

14
00:00:37,710 --> 00:00:38,920
AANG: Oof!

15
00:00:39,045 --> 00:00:42,006
But I believe Aang can save the world.

16
00:00:59,929 --> 00:01:01,890
OZAI: Come on out, Avatar!

17
00:01:02,015 --> 00:01:04,351
You can't hide in there forever!

18
00:01:11,483 --> 00:01:12,609
Toph, metalbend the rudder,

19
00:01:12,734 --> 00:01:14,444
so it's jammed in the turning position.

20
00:01:14,569 --> 00:01:16,613
The ship will spiral
and slam into the others.

21
00:01:16,738 --> 00:01:18,281
Got it.

22
00:01:19,949 --> 00:01:22,243
( SPITS )

23
00:01:22,369 --> 00:01:24,287
( STRAINING )

24
00:01:27,832 --> 00:01:28,958
CREW: ( GASPS )

25
00:01:34,464 --> 00:01:35,840
Have I ever mentioned how sweet it is

26
00:01:35,965 --> 00:01:37,717
that you invented metalbending?

27
00:01:37,842 --> 00:01:39,636
You could stand to mention it more.

28
00:01:48,686 --> 00:01:50,355
BOTH: ( SCREAMING )

29
00:01:55,318 --> 00:01:56,486
TOPH: ( SCREAMS )

30
00:01:56,611 --> 00:01:58,988
- SOKKA: Oh!
-( GRUNTS )

31
00:01:59,114 --> 00:02:02,075
( STRAINING )

32
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:03,660
My leg!

33
00:02:03,785 --> 00:02:06,830
- Hang on, Toph.
- Aye-aye, Captain.

34
00:02:21,511 --> 00:02:23,555
-( GRUNTS )
-( SCREAMS )

35
00:02:24,597 --> 00:02:27,183
Bye, space sword.

36
00:02:33,731 --> 00:02:35,150
( STRAINING )

37
00:02:35,275 --> 00:02:37,569
I don't think Boomerang
is coming back, Toph.

38
00:02:37,652 --> 00:02:39,612
It's looks like this is the end.

39
00:02:39,821 --> 00:02:41,489
CREW: ( GASPING )

40
00:02:43,491 --> 00:02:45,535
( METAL SCRAPING )

41
00:02:50,790 --> 00:02:54,169
How did that happen?
Did Boomerang come back?

42
00:02:54,294 --> 00:02:56,296
No, Suki did.

43
00:03:34,667 --> 00:03:36,419
-( THUNDER CRASHING )
-( SCREAMS )

44
00:03:46,513 --> 00:03:50,099
Come on out, little boy.
You're about to be―

45
00:03:50,183 --> 00:03:51,601
( GASPS )

46
00:04:07,450 --> 00:04:09,452
( GRUNTING )

47
00:04:09,577 --> 00:04:11,871
( THUDS, GROANS )

48
00:04:19,921 --> 00:04:23,299
( ROARS )

49
00:04:26,594 --> 00:04:28,888
( GASPING )

50
00:05:06,426 --> 00:05:07,677
Huh!

51
00:05:11,139 --> 00:05:12,807
Ah!

52
00:05:15,268 --> 00:05:16,311
( STRAINING )

53
00:05:16,436 --> 00:05:18,438
( GRUNTS )

54
00:05:26,613 --> 00:05:29,574
( CLANKING )

55
00:05:29,699 --> 00:05:32,452
MEN: ( GROANING )

56
00:05:54,349 --> 00:05:55,808
( GROANS )

57
00:06:16,204 --> 00:06:17,789
( GROANS )

58
00:06:17,997 --> 00:06:19,374
( GASPS )

59
00:06:19,499 --> 00:06:20,833
( PANTING )

60
00:06:20,958 --> 00:06:22,168
( FLAMES ROARING )

61
00:06:22,293 --> 00:06:24,212
AZULA: ( LAUGHS MANIACALLY )

62
00:06:24,504 --> 00:06:27,423
( GROANING )

63
00:06:28,758 --> 00:06:30,718
( GRUNTS )

64
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:35,348
I'd really rather our family physician

65
00:06:35,473 --> 00:06:37,975
look after little Zu Zu,
if you don't mind.

66
00:06:38,101 --> 00:06:39,769
( ELECTRICITY ZAPPING )

67
00:06:51,447 --> 00:06:54,075
AZULA: Zu Zu, you don't look so good.

68
00:06:55,118 --> 00:06:56,452
Hyah!

69
00:07:15,054 --> 00:07:16,305
( GRUNTS )

70
00:07:25,398 --> 00:07:27,734
There you are, filthy peasant.

71
00:07:48,129 --> 00:07:49,756
( WATER BUBBLING )

72
00:08:05,354 --> 00:08:06,773
BOTH: ( PANTING, COUGHING )

73
00:08:08,941 --> 00:08:10,359
( GROANS )

74
00:08:10,485 --> 00:08:12,904
( STRAINING )

75
00:08:14,822 --> 00:08:16,032
( GROANING )

76
00:08:33,132 --> 00:08:34,759
( SOFTLY ) Thank you, Katara.

77
00:08:35,343 --> 00:08:38,012
I think I'm the one
who should be thanking you.

78
00:08:41,432 --> 00:08:43,601
( HYPERVENTILATING )

79
00:08:44,811 --> 00:08:47,313
( SCREAMING )

80
00:08:50,358 --> 00:08:53,694
( SOBBING )

81
00:08:55,822 --> 00:08:58,825
( SCREAMS, SOBS CONTINUE )

82
00:09:31,107 --> 00:09:32,316
( GASPS )

83
00:09:36,279 --> 00:09:38,406
( CRASHING )

84
00:10:53,022 --> 00:10:54,649
( GASPS )

85
00:10:57,693 --> 00:10:58,903
AANG: ( IN DISTORTED VOICE ) Fire Lord Ozai,

86
00:10:59,028 --> 00:11:00,571
you and your forefathers

87
00:11:00,696 --> 00:11:02,490
have devastated the balance of this world,

88
00:11:02,615 --> 00:11:06,077
and now, you shall pay the ultimate price.

89
00:11:09,497 --> 00:11:11,999
( ROARING )

90
00:11:21,133 --> 00:11:23,511
( WATER SPLASHES )

91
00:11:31,811 --> 00:11:33,229
( GROANS )

92
00:11:40,903 --> 00:11:44,240
No. I am not gonna end it like this.

93
00:11:44,657 --> 00:11:47,201
Even with all power in the world,

94
00:11:47,410 --> 00:11:49,912
you are still weak.

95
00:12:09,557 --> 00:12:11,934
( HYPNOTIC CHANTING )

96
00:12:15,479 --> 00:12:19,275
LION TURTLE: In the era before the Avatar,

97
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:21,736
we bent not the elements,

98
00:12:21,861 --> 00:12:25,406
but the energy within ourselves.

99
00:12:52,641 --> 00:12:54,977
( RUMBLING )

100
00:13:03,736 --> 00:13:06,864
LION TURTLE: To bend another's energy,

101
00:13:07,031 --> 00:13:11,077
your own spirit must be unbendable,

102
00:13:11,202 --> 00:13:15,164
or you will be corrupted and destroyed.

103
00:13:43,109 --> 00:13:44,819
BOTH: ( GROAN )

104
00:13:50,699 --> 00:13:52,076
( GRUNTS WEAKLY )

105
00:13:52,159 --> 00:13:53,244
( GROANS )

106
00:13:53,327 --> 00:13:55,788
What? What did you do to me?

107
00:13:56,247 --> 00:13:58,082
I took away your firebending.

108
00:13:58,165 --> 00:14:01,794
You can't use it to hurt or
threaten anyone else ever again.

109
00:14:09,927 --> 00:14:12,721
( BREATHING DEEPLY )

110
00:14:52,261 --> 00:14:53,929
( CHATTERING )

111
00:15:07,359 --> 00:15:08,944
You did it!

112
00:15:09,069 --> 00:15:11,071
You should've seen yourself!
It was amazing!

113
00:15:11,197 --> 00:15:12,531
You were all like...

114
00:15:12,615 --> 00:15:14,950
( IMITATES ZAPPING, PUNCHING, EXPLOSIONS )

115
00:15:15,117 --> 00:15:16,619
...and the Fire Lord was all like...

116
00:15:16,702 --> 00:15:20,039
( IMITATES GROANING, CHOKING, MOANING )

117
00:15:20,414 --> 00:15:24,835
So, did you, you know, finish the job?

118
00:15:25,544 --> 00:15:28,255
I'm still alive.

119
00:15:29,632 --> 00:15:30,925
I learned there was another way

120
00:15:31,008 --> 00:15:32,718
to defeat him and restore balance.

121
00:15:33,093 --> 00:15:34,470
I took his bending away.

122
00:15:34,803 --> 00:15:36,889
Wow, who taught you that?

123
00:15:37,056 --> 00:15:38,682
A giant lion turtle.

124
00:15:38,807 --> 00:15:41,477
You have the craziest
adventures when you disappear.

125
00:15:42,436 --> 00:15:44,688
Well, look at you, buster.

126
00:15:44,772 --> 00:15:46,065
Now that your firebending is gone,

127
00:15:46,148 --> 00:15:48,901
I guess we should call
you the "Loser Lord".

128
00:15:49,526 --> 00:15:52,404
I am the Phoenix King.

129
00:15:52,488 --> 00:15:54,156
-( GROANING )
-( THUDS )

130
00:15:54,490 --> 00:15:56,575
Oh, sorry, didn't mean to offend you,

131
00:15:56,659 --> 00:15:58,994
Phoenix King of getting his butt-whooped.

132
00:15:59,370 --> 00:16:04,792
Yeah, or how about "King of...
The Guys Who Don't Win"?

133
00:16:05,042 --> 00:16:06,961
Leave the nicknames to us, honey.

134
00:16:27,523 --> 00:16:29,316
( GROANING )

135
00:16:29,441 --> 00:16:31,277
You need some help with that?

136
00:16:33,904 --> 00:16:36,073
Mai. You're okay.

137
00:16:36,991 --> 00:16:38,158
They let you out of prison?

138
00:16:38,284 --> 00:16:40,119
My uncle pulled some strings.

139
00:16:40,244 --> 00:16:43,080
And it doesn't hurt when
the new Fire Lord is your boyfriend.

140
00:16:43,163 --> 00:16:45,332
So, does this mean you
don't hate me anymore?

141
00:16:45,416 --> 00:16:48,919
I think it means
I actually kind of like you.

142
00:16:53,340 --> 00:16:56,635
But don't ever break up with me again.

143
00:17:05,978 --> 00:17:07,813
CROWD: ( MURMURING )

144
00:17:13,193 --> 00:17:14,653
- Dad!
- Dad!

145
00:17:18,657 --> 00:17:20,409
I heard what you two did.

146
00:17:20,743 --> 00:17:24,580
I am the proudest father in the world.

147
00:17:24,705 --> 00:17:27,875
And your mother would be proud, too.

148
00:17:29,918 --> 00:17:31,754
SOKKA: There's my favorite warriors.

149
00:17:31,879 --> 00:17:33,756
I have to admit,
I kinda missed the face paint.

150
00:17:33,964 --> 00:17:36,133
So, how's it feel to be
back in uniform again?

151
00:17:36,425 --> 00:17:38,010
It feels great!

152
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:40,929
Careful, Suki!

153
00:17:41,096 --> 00:17:43,724
Ty Lee's pretending to be
a Kyoshi Warrior again.

154
00:17:44,099 --> 00:17:45,225
It's okay.

155
00:17:45,351 --> 00:17:46,435
She's one of us now.

156
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:48,228
( YELPS )

157
00:17:48,354 --> 00:17:50,939
Yeah, the girls and I
really bonded in prison

158
00:17:51,106 --> 00:17:52,941
and after a few chi-blocking lessons,

159
00:17:53,067 --> 00:17:54,651
they said I could join their group.

160
00:17:54,777 --> 00:17:57,488
We're gonna be best friends forever.

161
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:08,165
I can't believe a year ago
my purpose in life

162
00:18:08,248 --> 00:18:10,084
was hunting you down and now...

163
00:18:10,501 --> 00:18:11,877
And now we're friends.

164
00:18:12,628 --> 00:18:15,506
Yeah. We are friends.

165
00:18:16,173 --> 00:18:19,134
I can't believe a year ago
I was still frozen in a block of ice.

166
00:18:19,593 --> 00:18:21,428
The world's so different now.

167
00:18:21,762 --> 00:18:24,223
And it's gonna be even more different.

168
00:18:24,431 --> 00:18:26,475
We'll rebuild it together.

169
00:18:37,152 --> 00:18:38,821
( GONG RINGING )

170
00:18:42,032 --> 00:18:44,910
CROWD: ( CHEERING )

171
00:18:45,244 --> 00:18:47,788
Please, the real hero...

172
00:18:47,913 --> 00:18:49,039
Is the Avatar.

173
00:18:51,917 --> 00:18:53,669
( CHEERING )

174
00:19:02,344 --> 00:19:05,931
ZUKO: Today, this war is finally over!

175
00:19:06,306 --> 00:19:09,852
( CHEERING )

176
00:19:10,144 --> 00:19:11,770
I promised my uncle that I would restore

177
00:19:11,895 --> 00:19:15,023
the honor of the Fire Nation, and I will.

178
00:19:15,357 --> 00:19:17,651
The road ahead of us is challenging.

179
00:19:17,985 --> 00:19:22,114
A hundred years of fighting
has left the world scarred and divided.

180
00:19:22,781 --> 00:19:24,533
But with the Avatar's help,

181
00:19:24,616 --> 00:19:26,910
we can get it back on the right path,

182
00:19:26,994 --> 00:19:30,706
and begin a new era of love and peace.

183
00:19:37,087 --> 00:19:40,340
All hail Fire Lord Zuko!

184
00:19:40,466 --> 00:19:42,801
CROWD: ( CHEERING )

185
00:20:18,712 --> 00:20:20,923
I should count myself lucky...

186
00:20:21,215 --> 00:20:23,342
The new Fire Lord has
graced me with his presence

187
00:20:23,467 --> 00:20:25,344
in my lowly prison cell.

188
00:20:25,594 --> 00:20:26,803
You should count yourself lucky

189
00:20:26,929 --> 00:20:29,348
that the Avatar spared your life.

190
00:20:29,765 --> 00:20:31,058
Hmm...

191
00:20:31,183 --> 00:20:33,852
Banishing me was the best thing
you could have done for my life.

192
00:20:34,186 --> 00:20:36,146
It put me on the right path.

193
00:20:37,314 --> 00:20:40,067
Perhaps your time in here
can do the same for you.

194
00:20:40,817 --> 00:20:43,445
Why are you really here?

195
00:20:43,570 --> 00:20:45,489
Because you're gonna tell me something.

196
00:20:47,783 --> 00:20:50,285
Where is my mother?

197
00:20:57,876 --> 00:20:59,920
( GRUNT OF EFFORT )

198
00:21:02,631 --> 00:21:04,174
( LAUGHING )

199
00:21:05,259 --> 00:21:07,636
APPA: ( GRUMBLING )

200
00:21:08,303 --> 00:21:12,099
( PLAYING CALMING MUSIC )

201
00:21:12,224 --> 00:21:13,684
( STOPS PLAYING )

202
00:21:16,979 --> 00:21:19,147
( MUSIC RESUMES )

203
00:21:20,857 --> 00:21:22,776
Zuko, stop moving!

204
00:21:22,901 --> 00:21:25,195
I'm trying to capture the moment.

205
00:21:26,029 --> 00:21:27,531
I wanted to do a painting,

206
00:21:27,656 --> 00:21:29,658
so we'd always remember
the good times together.

207
00:21:29,783 --> 00:21:32,244
That's very thoughtful of you, Sokka.

208
00:21:32,369 --> 00:21:35,038
Wait, why did you give me Momo's ears?

209
00:21:35,163 --> 00:21:36,748
SOKKA: Those are your hair loopies.

210
00:21:37,165 --> 00:21:39,585
At least you don't look like a porcupine.

211
00:21:39,668 --> 00:21:41,712
My hair is not that spiky.

212
00:21:41,795 --> 00:21:43,088
SUKI: I look like a man.

213
00:21:43,171 --> 00:21:45,257
TOPH: And why did you
paint me firebending?

214
00:21:45,507 --> 00:21:48,677
I thought it looked
more exciting that way.

215
00:21:48,760 --> 00:21:51,096
Oh, you think you could do
a better job, Momo?

216
00:21:51,471 --> 00:21:53,348
MOMO: ( CHATTERING )

217
00:21:53,765 --> 00:21:56,435
IROH: Hey, my belly
is not that big anymore...

218
00:21:56,560 --> 00:21:58,020
I've really trimmed down.

219
00:21:58,145 --> 00:22:00,022
TOPH: Well, I think you all look perfect!

220
00:22:00,147 --> 00:22:01,440
ALL: ( LAUGHING )

221
00:23:09,091 --> 00:23:11,093
( CLOSING THEME PLAYING )
